  "explanation": "The public failure shows three mismatches: cycle 4 input_axis_tready (1 vs 0), and cycles 8/9 output_axis_tdata (2 vs 1, 3 vs 2). The top-ranked patch directly resets data_out_reg (the output data register) on output clock reset, matching the zero-initialization trace. The next three patches stabilize cross-domain reset sequencing at the pointer synchronizers (lines 160, 110, 160), where zero state_edges at cycle 8 on output_axis_tdata indicate static dependency without proven dynamic causality. Patches 5 and 6 gate the input_axis_tready handshake (line 105) to suppress ready during output reset propagation, directly addressing the cycle 4 mismatch. Patch 7 qualifies output pointer reset with !input_rst_sync3 (line 160), and patch 8 couples output reset to write activity (line 160), both targeting the output data failures. All citations reference original source lines and the exact failing ports from the trace."
